    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "O'Mahony Walsh are delighted to present No. 19 Winterfield Close to the market. Built in 2022, this superb A-rated home offers three bedrooms, three bathrooms and five years remaining on its HomeBond guarantee. Set within the sought-after Castle Court development, overlooking a large green area and enjoying a sunny south-facing rear garden.\n\nThe heart of Whitechurch is just a short walk away, with St Patrick's National School, Whitechurch GAA, the community centre, a sauna and a coffee spot all close by. The combination of a welcoming village setting, modern comforts and an excellent position makes No. 19 a home well worth viewing.\n\nHallway (4.22m x 2.74m)\nA warm and inviting entrance hallway with access to all accommodation.\n\nGuest WC (1.61m x 1.53m)\nStylish guest WC with Aztec tiling, WC, WHB and a front aspect window.\n\nLiving Room (4.88m x 3.79m)\nSpacious living room with a front aspect window. This is the perfect space for spending time with family or relaxing after a hard day's work.\n\nOpen Plan Kitchen (3.83m x 2.96m)\nA bright, welcoming space centred on a fully fitted kitchen with generous worktops and excellent storage. Integrated appliances include a full-size Nord Mende fridge and freezer, Whirlpool dishwasher, Nord Mende double oven and grill, Nord Mende hob and Faber extractor fan. A white ceramic sink with a rose gold tap adds a distinctive finishing touch, while a double larder and concealed pull-out bins keep the kitchen practical and uncluttered. The rear-facing window overlooks the south-facing garden and fills the room with natural light.\n\nDining Area (3.84m x 3.67m) / Family Room (3.67m x 2.80m)\nFlowing from the kitchen, the spacious dining and family area offers a flexible setting for everyday living and entertaining. Double doors open onto the rear garden, bringing natural light into the open-plan space.\n\nUtility (1.69m x 1.34m)\nA practical utility room with a Nord Mende washing machine and dryer, and a fitted worktop, providing useful space for laundry and storage.\n\nStairs & Landing (3.67m x 2.85m)\nA carpeted turn staircase leads to a landing with laminate flooring. The landing provides access to a partly floored attic with lighting and power sockets.\n\nMaster Bedroom (3.82m x 3.66m)\nA generously sized double bedroom with spacious mirrored sliding wardrobes. The front-facing window overlooks the green area and brings in plenty of natural light.\n\nEn-Suite (3.01m x 1.03m)\nA fully tiled en-suite with a separate shower, WC and wash hand basin.\n\nBedroom 2 (3.68m x 3.25m)\nA double bedroom with a rear aspect window overlooking the sunny south facing garden.\n\nBedroom 3 (2.98m x 2.48m)\nDouble bedroom with a front aspect window providing plenty of natural light.\n\nFamily Bathroom (2.84m x 1.80m)\nA well-appointed bathroom featuring a 3-piece suite, tiled flooring, partly tiled walls and a side aspect window.\n\nGarden Details\nFront:\nA cobblelock driveway provides off-street parking for two cars, with hedging along the boundaries. Gated side access connects to a pathway that wraps around the property.\n\nRear:\nThe sunny, south-facing rear garden is mainly laid to lawn, with a patio area ideal for outdoor dining. Timber fencing encloses the boundaries, while an outside tap and outdoor power socket add convenience.\n\nHeating\nAir to water\nUnderfloor Heating on ground floor\n\nBER Details\nBER: A2 BER No: 114611635 Energy Performance Indicator: 39.71kWh/m2/yr"
      },
